# UI Component Rules

Screens orchestrate. Components render. Never dump a full layout into a screen file, and never rebuild a primitive that already exists in `src/components/common`.

## Use our custom components (required)

Always compose UI from `src/components/common`. Do not use the React Native / library equivalent when a wrapper exists.

| Need              | Use                                      | Do not use                                      |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Screen shell      | `MainWrapper`                            | Raw `SafeAreaView` / `ImageBackground` as the screen root |
| Header            | `AppHeader`                              | A custom title/back row                         |
| Text              | `AppText` (`weight`, `size`)             | RN `Text`                                       |
| Image             | `AppImage`                               | RN `Image` or `expo-image` directly             |
| Avatar            | `UserAvatar`                             | A one-off image + initials row                  |
| Button / CTA      | `Button` (`primary` \| `outlined` \| `text`) | Hand-rolled `TouchableOpacity` + text      |
| Text field        | `TextInput`                              | RN `TextInput`                                  |
| Select            | `Dropdown`                               | A custom picker list                            |
| Search            | `SearchBar`                              | A custom search row                             |
| Bottom sheet      | `BottomSheet` (+ `BottomSheetFlatList` / `BottomSheetScrollView` / `BottomSheetTextInput`) | `@gorhom/bottom-sheet` in a feature file |
| Progress / charts | `ProgressBar`, `Seekbar`, `Piechart`, `BarChart`, `StreakCalendar` | One-off chart widgets when these fit |
| FAQ row           | `FAQItem`                                | A custom accordion row                          |

Import them from `src/components/common` (the file or the barrel). Extend a common component if you need a variant — do not fork it into a feature folder.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<MainWrapper>
  <AppHeader title="Settings" showBack showIcons={false} />
  <AppImage source={uri} style={styles.cover} resizeMode="cover" />
  <AppText weight="SemiBold" size="md">Title</AppText>
  <Button title="Continue" onPress={onContinue} />
</MainWrapper>

// ❌ BAD
<SafeAreaView>
  <Text>Title</Text>
  <Image source={{ uri }} />
  <TouchableOpacity onPress={onContinue}><Text>Continue</Text></TouchableOpacity>
</SafeAreaView>
```

Styling: colors from `palette` (`src/theme`). Spacing, radius, and type size via `scale` / `verticalScale` / `moderateScale` from `react-native-size-matters`. `StyleSheet.create` at the bottom of the file. No hardcoded hex. If a color is missing, add it to `palette` first.

## Where files live

```
src/screens/<stack>/ScreenName.tsx     # route orchestrator only
src/components/common/                 # app-wide primitives (table above)
src/components/<feature>/              # UI owned by one screen or flow
src/components/<feature>/<TabName>/    # one folder per tab on a tabbed screen
```

- Feature folders: `snake_case`, named after the screen or flow.
- Component files: `PascalCase`.
- New screen-specific UI goes in `src/components/<feature>/`, not under `common/`.
- `common/` is only for widgets reused across flows.
- Colocate shared `types.ts` / `constants.ts` in the feature folder when more than one file needs them.
- Each feature folder has an `index.ts` barrel. Screens import from the barrel.

```
# ✅ screen composes common primitives + feature barrel
import MainWrapper from "../../components/common/MainWrapper";
import { SectionCard, ItemList } from "../../components/<feature>";

# ❌ entire screen layout written inside screens/
# ❌ a one-screen widget dumped into components/common
```

## How to break a screen

The screen file should only:

1. Wrap with `MainWrapper` (and `AppHeader` when there is a title/back).
2. Call hooks — never `api/` directly (see `api-integration.mdc`).
3. Compose sections and pass UI-ready props.
4. Handle navigation, refresh, and loading/error shells.

Split a new file when **any** of these is true:

| Split as       | When                                                            |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `*Card`        | A titled visual block (summary, quote, status, promo)           |
| `*Item`        | One row in a list — presentational, primitive props             |
| `*List`        | Maps data → `*Item`; owns section title / empty spacing         |
| `*Tab`         | Full body of one tab scene                                      |
| `*Modal`       | Feature-only overlay                                            |
| `*BottomSheet` | Feature-only sheet **content** (chrome still from common `BottomSheet`) |
| `*ScreenLayout`| Shared wrapper + header + content padding for a multi-screen flow |

**List / Item:** the list maps and passes primitives. The item does not fetch, does not read route params, and does not import other feature cards.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
items.map((item) => (
  <RowItem
    key={item?.id}
    title={item?.title ?? ""}
    subtitle={item?.subtitle ?? ""}
    onPress={() => onPressItem?.(item?.id)}
  />
));

// ❌ BAD — item takes the whole API object and fetches inside the row
<RowItem item={item} />
```

**Tabs:** the screen owns `MainWrapper` + the tab bar. Each scene is `src/components/<feature>/<TabName>/<TabName>Tab.tsx`, with that tab’s cards in the same folder.

Do not extract a 5-line wrapper used once with no name in the design. Do extract as soon as a block has its own layout, title, or data.

## Component file shape

- One component per file. Functional component, typed props, **default export**.
- Props type in the same file unless shared — then `types.ts` in the feature folder.
- Optional-chain any API-derived value (`item?.name ?? ""`).
- Keep list items lightweight: no queries, no large hooks. Fetch in a hook; pass props down.

```tsx
const FeatureCard: React.FC<Props> = ({ title, onPress }) => {
  return (
    <TouchableOpacity style={styles.container} onPress={onPress} activeOpacity={0.7}>
      <AppText weight="SemiBold" size="md">{title}</AppText>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
};

export default FeatureCard;
```

Barrel `index.ts` re-exports defaults as named exports.

## Hard rules

- Always use the custom common components in the table above — never the RN/library equivalent.
- Screens do not contain large visual trees — extract `*Card` / `*List` / `*Item` / `*Tab`.
- Feature UI does not live in `screens/` or in `components/common/` (unless it is a true app-wide primitive).
- Do not hardcode hex colors; add a token to `palette` if missing.
- Do not import from `src/api/` in a presentational component; the screen/tab uses a hook.
- New screens go in `src/screens/<stack>/` and must be registered on the matching navigator.
